1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,700
A crash changes the corridor in seconds.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,000
Test the response before it reaches drivers.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,500
Ripple structures a Transport Department incident notice.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Then it builds response options for the operator.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,600
Aberdeen: archived detectors show the slowdown.

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:33,000
Ripple compares options in a seeded traffic model.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,500
No advice and the targeted plan tie.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Ripple holds the recommendation.

9
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:49,000
Tuen Mun: archived speeds from fixed detectors.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The observed slowdown unfolds across the corridor.

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:01,500
Across 18 modelled conditions, targeted advice

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:10,000
leads in 17, with 4.3% less simulated total delay.

13
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,000
Blanket advice adds 37% modelled delay.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The narrow plan is the strongest tested candidate.

15
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:23,000
The operator reviews, then approves.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
AI proposes. Simulation measures. People decide.

17
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,000
Ripple. Test the detour.
